{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# J9 — Make the DC transport actually drive a writing reconcile pass\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nStory J7 [rebar:b4e3-1de0-3188-40a1] landed the DC backend's port conformance and made it reachable\nthrough config, then drove it against a REAL Jira Data Center instance for the first time (GitHub\nActions run 30604756524). The writing path CRASHES:\n\n    ERROR: reconcile_once raised: 'JiraDataCenterTransport' object has no attribute\n    'set_entity_property'\n\n`--mode dry-run` passes; `--mode bootstrap-strict` exits 1. So epic e369's headline capability —\nJira Server/Data Center support — does not work yet, and the epic cannot honestly close without this.\n\nFiled as [rebar:a357-b747-ece9-4cf5]; this story is its implementation.\n\n## The root cause is a PORT defect, and the gap is TEN methods\n\nAn AST audit over `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/*.py` — collecting every method invoked on a\n`client`/`transport` receiver, diffed against `JiraDataCenterTransport`'s methods and against every\nProtocol in `_backend.py` — measured the real gap:\n\n**Called by the core, ABSENT from the DC transport (10):**\n`delete_issue`, `get_comments`, `get_issue_by_rest`, `get_issue_links`, `get_parent_map`,\n`remove_label`, `set_entity_property`, `set_issue_property`, `set_reporter`,\n`validate_assignee_exists`.\n\n**Declared on NO Protocol in `_backend.py`: the same 10.**\n\nAll ten ARE implemented for Cloud, spread across `adapters/jira/acli_rest.py`, `acli.py` and\n`acli_graph.py`.\n\nSo `set_entity_property` is not \"the\" missing method — it is the FIRST one a live writing pass\nhappened to reach. Nine more sit behind it. **Implementing only `set_entity_property` would move the\ncrash one call deeper** and produce another red run, looking like progress while the capability stays\nbroken.\n\n`TicketTransport` declares six members (`create_issue`, `get_issue`, `update_issue`,\n`transition_issue_by_name`, `add_label`, `search_issues`); the core calls fifteen. The port describes\n40% of its own requirement. That is exactly why `isinstance` conformance, the backend contract suite,\nand 1636 reconciler unit tests were all green against a transport that cannot complete a writing pass.\n**Conformance to an incomplete port proves less than it appears to** — the same class as J6's\n`add_label` defect, where the only oracle was a fake mirroring the author's assumption.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Implement the missing transport methods on `JiraDataCenterTransport` against DC's REST v2 API,\n   reading each Cloud counterpart first rather than inventing a shape. `set_entity_property` is\n   Cloud's alias for `set_issue_property`, which PUTs to\n   `/rest/api/3/issue/{key}/properties/{prop}` with the value sent **verbatim as the body** — an\n   earlier Cloud bug (0b27) wrapped it in `{\"value\": ...}` and silently stored the wrong shape, so\n   copy the corrected contract, not the intuition. DC is REST **v2**.\n2. Where a method is genuinely not applicable to DC, it must raise a clear `NotImplementedError`\n   naming the DC limitation — never be left absent to fail as `AttributeError` mid-pass. Each such\n   decision needs evidence, not assumption.\n3. Declare the transport surface on the port so a backend missing a member fails at construction\n   rather than at runtime, and add a STRUCTURAL TEST that every transport method the core calls is\n   declared. That test is what converts \"I found ten\" into \"the eleventh cannot be introduced\n   silently\", and is the part that stops this class of defect recurring on the next backend.\n\n**Alternative rejected:** implement `set_entity_property` alone. It fixes one crash, leaves nine, and\nleaves the port still misdescribing what the core needs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py` — implement\n  `set_entity_property`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_backend.py` — declare it on `TicketTransport`.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/backend_support.py` — `FakeTransport` gains the method, since the\n  fake must satisfy the widened port (it is the contract suite's stand-in).\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` — a structural test for the audit: every transport attribute the\n  core reaches for is declared on the Protocol.\n- `tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_reconcile_pass.py` — already written by J7; it is the oracle and\n  must go from FAIL to PASS unmodified. **Do not weaken it to accommodate the fix.**\n\n## Testing\n\n- unit: `set_entity_property` issues the right REST call, asserted against a fake client — including\n  that the property KEY and VALUE reach the endpoint intact, since a silently wrong shape breaks\n  correlation without raising.\n- structural: the core-call-sites-vs-Protocol audit is a TEST, not a one-off grep, so a future core\n  module reaching for an undeclared transport method fails CI. Give it teeth with a synthetic case,\n  mirroring `test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py::test_checker_flags_a_synthetic_violation`.\n- live: J7's `test_reconcile_pass.py` must pass in the `jira-dc-harness` CI job.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] every method the core calls on a transport is EITHER implemented on `JiraDataCenterTransport`\n      OR raises `NotImplementedError` naming the DC limitation — no member may be simply absent, so\n      no call site can fail with `AttributeError` mid-pass. The ten measured absentees are\n      `delete_issue`, `get_comments`, `get_issue_by_rest`, `get_issue_links`, `get_parent_map`,\n      `remove_label`, `set_entity_property`, `set_issue_property`, `set_reporter`,\n      `validate_assignee_exists`\n- [ ] `set_entity_property` specifically is implemented and unit-tested, with the test asserting the\n      property key and value reach the REST layer INTACT — Cloud bug 0b27 stored `{\"value\": x}`\n      instead of `x`, and a wrong shape breaks correlation WITHOUT raising, so \"it did not error\" is\n      not evidence here\n- [ ] the transport surface the core requires is declared on the port, so a transport missing a\n      member fails an `isinstance` check at construction rather than at runtime mid-pass, asserted\n      by test\n- [ ] a structural test asserts every transport method the core reconciler calls is declared on the\n      Protocol, and that test is proven to FIRE on a synthetic undeclared method\n- [ ] [operator-attested] a full writing reconcile pass (`bootstrap-strict`) against the J5 harness converges with no\n      unhandled exception — J7's `test_dc_reconcile_pass_raises_no_unhandled_exception` passes for a\n      WRITING mode, not only dry-run\n- [ ] [operator-attested] an immediately repeated writing pass writes nothing (idempotence) —\n      J7's `test_a_repeated_dc_reconcile_pass_writes_nothing` passes\n- [ ] [operator-attested] a DC-created ticket carries `creation_channel == 'jira'` — J7's\n      `test_a_dc_created_ticket_carries_the_shared_jira_provenance` passes\n- [ ] the three live tests above pass WITHOUT any edit to `test_reconcile_pass.py` (`git diff` shows\n      that file unchanged) — the oracle is not adjusted to fit the fix\n\n## Note on the moved criteria\n\nThe three `[operator-attested]` live criteria were J7's. They are relocated here, not dropped: J7\ncannot satisfy them (its own scope is landed and verified), and this is the story whose fix makes them\npassable. Epic e369 therefore still requires a proven live writing pass before it closes."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785475468637444001,"uuid":"c6a89884-6a98-49df-830a-8ad52f27f81f"}